The getter is already a single direct call into the field-lookup helper and is not on the hot decode path, so no safe transformation can lower its cost; I kept the accessor call unchanged to guarantee identical behavior and the 1.000 baseline.

```cpp
    FIT_UINT32 GetSurfaceInterval(void) const
    {
        return GetFieldUINT32Value(4, 0, FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD);
    }
```